& [Purpose]
  + bind one supplied effectless inner launch plan and one explicit detached plan-compilation authorization to one exact validated NHC-03 bundle
  + make later single-attempt launch execution planning deterministic inspectable cancellation-aware and ambiguity-preserving without observing executables creating a process loading a model or claiming runtime state

& [Profiles]
  + [NHLP-001] request profile is cantor-nested-inner-launch-plan-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-nested-inner-launch-plan-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-nested-inner-launch-plan-verification/0.1
  + [NHLP-002] strict compact UTF-8 JSON denies unknown duplicate and trailing properties and is bounded to 1048576 bytes depth 28 fields 384 text 2048 and evidence 32

& [UpstreamBinding]
  + [NHLP-003] the complete supplied NHC-03 request envelope and verification must validate unchanged before any launch plan exists
  + [NHLP-004] all upstream inner session Cantor process artifact instance authorization identities digests lifecycle authority denials unresolved truths signature state and effects exactly equal the validated NHC-03 bundle and receive one domain-separated bundle digest
  + [NHLP-005] NHC-03 supplied_descriptor_and_key_cryptographic_correspondence_only authority fifteen denials ten unresolved truths and all-zero effects remain conserved

& [PlanIdentityAndTarget]
  + [NHLP-006] launch-plan identity is a nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing SemanticId distinct from all ten NHC-03 bound identities and the launch-plan authorization identity
  + [NHLP-007] plan state is proposed_effectless; target profile is direct_no_shell; executable and working-directory references are bounded opaque SemanticIds and prove no file presence bytes trust support or admission
  + [NHLP-008] argv is one through 32 ordered bounded strings with no empty element; environment is zero through 32 unique uppercase key names with supplied opaque value references; stdin stdout and stderr declarations are exact closed enums and no ambient PATH shell or environment inheritance exists
  + [NHLP-009] plan digest is domain-separated deterministic and self-excluding

& [Ceilings]
  + [NHLP-010] context memory threads and GPU ceilings exactly equal the NHC-03 proposed instance while startup and runtime milliseconds are 1 through 86400000 output bytes are 1 through 1073741824 descendants are 0 through 64 and cancellation grace milliseconds are 1 through 600000
  + [NHLP-011] ceilings do not prove current capacity compatibility availability executable support or successful runtime fit

& [PlanAuthorization]
  + [NHLP-012] authorization has its own distinct UUID-bearing identity and exact issuer subject-inner-Cantor plan action inner_launch_plan_compile policy SHA256 nonce SHA256 sequence lower and upper one-attempt zero-retry bindings
  + [NHLP-013] an exact Ed25519 public key and detached signature verify over the domain-separated canonical payload including the complete NHC-03 bundle digest plan identity target argv environment streams ceilings cancellation terminal grammar and every authorization field
  + [NHLP-014] accepted disposition is authorized_for_later_single_attempt_plan with consumption state unconsumed and authority supplied_key_cryptographic_launch_plan_authorization_only
  + [NHLP-015] correspondence proves no policy governance signer competence key custody revocation freshness current sequence executable truth or permission for this compiler to create a process

& [CancellationAndTerminalFaults]
  + [NHLP-016] request cancellation state is none_requested and compilation performs no cancellation; later grammar permits prelaunch_cancel_requested post_boundary_cancel_requested and terminal_cancelled only as distinct states
  + [NHLP-017] later terminal grammar is exactly prelaunch_refused launch_blocked launch_fault timed_out cancelled exit_success exit_failure and unknown_after_boundary
  + [NHLP-018] only prelaunch_refused or launch_blocked before creation may assert launch_may_have_occurred false; every uncertain post-boundary outcome preserves launch_may_have_occurred and load_may_have_occurred true-or-unknown and never asserts cleanup success
  + [NHLP-019] retry authorization consumption rollback quarantine recovery owner stream custody and process cleanup remain unresolved for NHC-05 or another separately signed physical contract

& [RequestEnvelopeAndVerification]
  + [NHLP-020] one through 32 unique evidence references and exactly twelve current unresolved truths are required: executable_file_presence_not_observed executable_bytes_not_reacquired working_directory_not_observed host_resource_fit_not_verified policy_governance_not_verified key_custody_revocation_freshness_not_verified current_sequence_not_observed model_not_loaded process_not_launched streams_not_owned cancellation_not_executed and terminal_outcome_not_observed
  + [NHLP-021] compilation emits authorized_effectless_launch_plan_only the unchanged request domain-separated request and envelope digests and exactly eighteen denials: artifact_file_observation artifact_byte_reacquisition artifact_download artifact_install model_load_attempt model_load_completion runtime_observation provider_call inference process_launch launch_plan_execution cancellation_execution stream_custody shared_attention persistence workspace_mutation remote_access and external_effect
  + [NHLP-022] equal valid requests compile byte identically; verification reports eight upstream operational identities ten operational identities twelve bound identities eighteen denials twelve current unresolved truths signature correspondence true and all effects zero; retained evidence double replays exact request envelope verification and manifest
  + [NHLP-023] upstream identity target argv environment stream ceiling authorization sequence cancellation terminal unresolved denial authority digest or fully redigested semantic mutation fails closed with typed faults and no partial output
  + [NHLP-024] production performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model MCP Git workspace persistence remote cleanup cancellation or external effect action

& [Acceptance]
  + [NHLP-A01] source audit delineation data dual threat seven-fold canonical explosion justification solution plan matrix phase lock proof review and satisfaction signature agree exactly
  + [NHLP-A02] safe Rust exports strict forms validation compilation domain-separated digests detached Ed25519 verification and ambiguity-preserving terminal forms using existing dependencies only
  + [NHLP-A03] focused positive deterministic adversarial and fully redigested-laundering tests plus two bounded CLIs four-file retained evidence and a separate verifier pass debug and overflow-checked release
  + [NHLP-A04] exact workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format recursive evidence attribution remote-equal publication and post-push replay pass
  + [NHLP-A05] executable observation policy governance actual plan consumption process creation model load runtime provider inference cancellation stream custody NHC-05 custody NHC-06 attention live models remote deployment and every effect remain separately governed

& [Invalidation]
  + source predecessor profile identity target argv environment stream ceiling authorization cancellation terminal unresolved denial authority lifecycle digest effect dependency requirement support or attribution drift
